---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Mixture of Limits"
  description="About: Mixture of Limits: Navigation Law for Computer Intelligence. OpenIE research study. Readable paper, PDF, and interactive figures. board_synth_claimed=false."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Paper 3 · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Mixture of Limits
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Navigation law for computer intelligence: floors where more bits stop buying outcomes.
      Compression and predictive formulas beat excess enumeration. Soft-ref constructive existence
      in software (~29 VERIFIED prove criteria) is claimable; FPGA and board package energy are not.
      OpenIE map (paper intro): <a href="https://stack.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">stack</a>,
      <a href="https://compute.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">compute</a>,
      <a href="https://knowledge.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">knowledge</a>,
      <a href="https://synthesis.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">synthesis</a>,
      <a href="https://research.openie.dev" class="text-brand-cyan">research</a>—Mixture of Limits navigates floors across that family.
      §8.7–§8.14: SOTA at the plateau—once VoI is zero past the floor, optimize energy/compute (Lookup → Formula → Solver → Model LAST). Plateau options include SSM/MoE efficiency, DeepSeek, Xiaomi MiMo, Qwen, Sarvam, and transmission / gearing / cascade / memory-context / test-time techniques—field reports, not board joules.
      §11: dual-phase roadmap—bounded micro-perception → typed AST, then the Mixture of Limits cascade; O(1) meta-routing; Primitive Distillation; Tier 0/1/2 meters (`measured_j` only when Metered); DX roadmap, not claimed shipped product.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
      Status: research study, not a journal final. Figures under /living/mol/ are companions.
      Analytical OpCounter / catalog estimates are estimates, not board power.
      Soft-ref path: <code class="text-brand-cyan">board_synth_claimed=false</code>; Landauer is a labeled estimate;
      package <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code> only when Metered.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion-laws">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion laws</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Catalog triad: <strong class="text-brand-white">Navigation</strong> (this study) ·
        <a href="/papers/ni/" class="text-brand-cyan">Commit</a> (Notational Intelligence as Commit Law) ·
        <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="text-brand-cyan">Economic done</a> (Satiation and Scarcity after Free AI).
        See <a href="/#companion-laws" class="text-brand-cyan">catalog triad</a>.
      </p>
    </div>


    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/mol/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/mol/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/mol.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/living/mol/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Interactive figures
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 glass-card p-6 space-y-3">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Paths</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/papers/mol/</span> → study prose</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/pdfs/mol.pdf</span> → downloadable study PDF (regenerate via scripts/generate-pdfs.sh)</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/living/mol/</span> → interactive figures (not the paper)</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Measurement bounds</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Analytical OpCounter ≠ board power. Landauer estimate labeled.
        Soft-ref prove path: <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j=None</code> unless Metered;
        <code class="text-brand-cyan">board_synth_claimed=false</code>. Soft-ref constructive existence is software, not FPGA/board package energy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
